{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtActionInjective","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion.sum_sq_of_numSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion.sum_sq_of_numSYT","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtWedderburnCriterion.lean#L102-L114","doc":"**The residue is combinatorial.** Restating the criterion's hypothesis through\n`dim_k S^μ = #SYT(μ)`: the open input is the RSK identity `Σ_{μ ⊢ n} (#SYT μ)² = n!`, a statement\nabout tableaux with no algebra in it.\n\nAnyone who proves the tableau identity — combinatorially or otherwise — gets the algebra\nisomorphism from `spechtEquiv_of_sum_sq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion.spechtEquiv_of_sum_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion.spechtEquiv_of_sum_sq","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtWedderburnCriterion.lean#L90-L100","doc":"**The algebra isomorphism, conditional on the dimension count.**\n\n`k[S_n] ≃ₐ[k] ∏_{μ ⊢ n} End_k(S^μ)`, partition-indexed, with block `μ` acting on `S^μ`. This is\nthe shape `sn_isotypic_specht_split` wants (modulo `End_k(S^μ) ≃ₐ Matrix (Fin (dim S^μ)) k`,\nwhich is a basis choice). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion.spechtProduct_bijective_of_sum_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion.spechtProduct_bijective_of_sum_sq","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtWedderburnCriterion.lean#L72-L88","doc":"**The criterion.** `spechtProduct` is bijective as soon as the block dimensions sum to `n!`.\n\nEverything else W1+W3 asks for is already in place: the map is partition-indexed by\nconstruction (so there is no labelling to choose), each block is `End_k(S^μ)` with `dim S^μ` the\nSpecht dimension (so the sizes are right by construction), and the commutant is the base field\n(W2, #5139) — the three items the `SnWedderburnPartitionBridge` residual lists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion.surjective_of_injective_of_finrank_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion.surjective_of_injective_of_finrank_eq","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtWedderburnCriterion.lean#L59-L70","doc":"An injective linear map between finite-dimensional spaces of equal dimension is onto.\n\nMathlib has the endomorphism case but not this one at the pinned version (`exact?` fails on the\nstatement); it is two steps — injectivity preserves the rank, and a full-rank submodule is\neverything. ","signatureChunk":0}]}